# Contributing

Open an issue before large changes. Never include passwords, session files,
tokens, workout exports, location data or unredacted logs. Use synthetic data.

Create a Python 3.12+ virtual environment, then run:
```text
python -m pip install -e ".[dev,remote]"
python -m pytest -q
```

Create a feature branch, make changes, submit a pull request, pass checks, then
merge. Do not push directly to the default branch. Describe behavior and tests.
Preserve fixed operation allowlists, explicit units, bounded responses, local
OAuth consent, PKCE, audience validation and separate write permissions. Do not
add arbitrary endpoints. Update documentation and CHANGELOG; synchronize
VERSION and pyproject.toml. Installation regenerates the local interpreter path
in the plugin manifest; do not commit a machine-specific path.

CI and default tests must remain offline. Live checks are opt-in:
`python scripts/verify_live.py`; they read an account but print only check results.
Verify unauthenticated remote calls return 401. Never disable TLS verification.
For vulnerabilities, use GitHub private reporting if available or contact the
maintainer privately before publishing details. Contributions use the MIT license.
